# module MSBuild checkout integration

Detect the lexicographically first root `.csproj` or `.fsproj`. `Export.Path` is the
consumer-root-relative project file or directory in the one submodule checkout; a directory must
contain exactly one root project file. This adapter never clones, copies, or removes that source.

# decision One generated targets file and one marked project import

`deps/git-a2a.targets` contains sorted `ProjectReference` blocks and is wholly owned by git-a2a.
The consumer project receives exactly `<Import Project="deps/git-a2a.targets" Label="git-a2a" />`
before its closing element. Each block excludes the checkout project's C# and F# sources from the
consumer SDK glob before adding the reference. Remove deletes only owned content.

# invariant Checkout composition and saved language variant

Read-only Capability rejects empty, `.`, absolute, and escaping paths as typed not-wirable.
Detection returns `msbuild-csharp` or `msbuild-fsharp`; the lifecycle persists and verifies it.
Pull resolves the checked-out project with `dotnet restore` after writing the reference, without
building the entire consumer. Remove restores the remaining consumer graph after deleting only
owned integration. Inspect reports an absent or ambiguous checkout project. Commit and checkout
management belong to the submodule adapter.

# test Golden lifecycle

Tests cover C# and F# detection, file/directory project paths, private editor idempotence,
Inspect, foreign-content repair, byte-restoring removal, read-only Capability, and missing
checkout projects.
